SM(530,{"n":"1 Corinthians 2-3","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/1 Corinthians 2-3.mp3","d":2111.8,"s":[[0.16,"Come and study Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.08,"Father Stephen is a former Protestant pastor and Bible teacher in the Reformed Church, but now an Orthodox priest, serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[20.96,"These things we also speak not in words which man's wisdom teaches, but which the Holy Spirit teaches, comparing spiritual things with spiritual."],[29.36,"But the m natural man does not receive the things of the Spirit of God, for they are foolishness to him, nor can he know them because they are spiritually discerned."],[38.64,"But he who is spiritual judges all things, yet he himself is rightly judged by no one."],[44.56,"For who has known the mind of the Lord that he may instruct him?"],[47.84,"But we have the mind of Christ."],[55.04,"So now he's talking, he's gone through a couple of things you shouldn' got to."],[59.04,"Right now, wisdom that man's word teaches."],[59.84,"That's philosophy What's that?"],[64.5,"Saying, you know what?"],[65.78,"The philosophers, who might want to jump in here on my critique of paganism."],[71.72,"And say, yeah, you're right, all that's nonsense."],[74.22,"We're more enlightened."],[75.34,"They don't have it either."],[77.76,"They don't have it either."],[79.04,"In fact, they can't perceive it."],[81.6,"Why? Well, one of the things we have to remember, and English translations do a lousy job with this."],[87.86,"They almost never capitalize spiritual."],[90.9,"When we hear the word spiritual in English, like I use the phrase jokingly, spiritual but not religious."],[96.98,"When we hear spiritual, we think of Marianne Williamson."],[100.82,"You know. They're not going to lose us our tax exempt status if I criticize her, since she's a presidential candidate right now"],[101.74,"Okay. By the time this airs, she probably won't be."],[109.82,"So crystal power."],[113.71,"Or you know, um, this kind of vaguely watered down Gnostic nonsense."],[120.0,"New age spirituality and all this."],[122.74,"And that's not what spiritual means in the Bible."],[125.38,"Spiritual means referring to the spirit, capital S."],[130.18,"Okay. The Holy Spirit."],[131.9,"And so what he's saying is, you know, yeah, the philosophers can go out and they can tell you all about the natural man, the person who's according to nature."],[139.8,"He they could go out and tell you all about the natural world."],[143.59,"It's not really spot on, but it's the best you can get in fourth century BC Greece"],[143.61,"Read Aristotle's Parts of Animals."],[150.89,"The closest thing to science you're gonna find."],[152.81,"They could tell you about all these things."],[154.87,"But they can't tell you about the things of God."],[157.67,"They can't tell you about the things of the spirit because they don't have the Holy Spirit, so they can't understand them."],[165.25,"These are things, these are truths that are on a plane and in a realm."],[168.79,"They're from the age to come."],[170.79,"St. Paul has already said, that they don't have access to."],[174.07,"And so they seem foolishness to them."],[176.39,"They're gonna want to come and laugh at them and laugh at you."],[179.85,"But they can't judge you."],[181.62,"Why? Well, who are they to judge the mind of God?"],[186.1,"But any philosopher, if you say, Hey, can you with your human mind judge the mind of God"],[186.12,"Yeah, they've got a brain, it's a human brain."],[192.52,"They'd be like, No."],[195.94,"Logically, no. So that's what he's saying."],[198.2,"And he's so saying, because the Holy Spirit is in you."],[202.74,"We're not, and we're talking about these things, we're not talking about your brain when we talk about your mind."],[208.82,"We're talking about the mind of Christ, which you have because, again, the Holy Spirit dwells in you."],[216.1,"Holy Spirit is the Spirit of God."],[218.18,"Holy Spirit is the Spirit of Christ."],[220.26,"So he knows the mind of Christ."],[222.1,"He knows the mind of God."],[224.91,"If he's dwelling within you, you have access to all that."],[228.19,"And a philosopher who doesn't have the Holy Spirit can't judge that."],[229.23,"He doesn't understand it"],[236.41,"It would be like, you know, having an eight-year-old try and and uh tell you if you did a good job solving a calculus problem."],[244.99,"He doesn't know."],[246.49,"He can't do that."],[247.69,"He's he's gone through."],[249.39,"Here's all the places where you're going and seeking after wisdom and you're seeking after understanding."],[256.68,"And you're digging in the wrong place."],[259.74,"It's not there to be found."],[262.56,"In any of these places."],[264.16,"The place where it's to be found is the Holy Spirit who's dwelling in you."],[268.56,"And it has been given to you freely."],[270.64,"That's the same"],[272.18,"Had to pay a large sum of money to get initiated into these things, too."],[277.54,"Paul says, I didn't come and charge you money to baptize you, to preach the gospel to you."],[287.62,"So this is what he's laid out."],[292.12,"I came to you and I I know there's nothing about me to recommend me to you."],[296.85,"There's nothing about me that would make you say, I want what that Paul guy's got."],[302.71,"Because he's living this hugely successful life."],[305.27,"And you know, it's like the guys in the infomercials with their money-making secrets."],[309.03,"It's always like them on a boat with a couple of models, you know."],[313.05,"Like that,'s not St."],[314.29,"Paul isn't. Saying here, hey, you want to have this lifestyle."],[318.52,"Um, in fact, his lifestyle was pretty lousy, and he was open with them about it."],[322.65,"He says, But what I gave you is of ultimate value."],[328.33,"And these other places where you're looking there in Corinth in your culture, there's nothing to be found for you there."],[336.49,"Except destruction. And you're forsaking everything you're really looking for by doing it, by going there and looking for it."],[346.89,"So we have a little time left, so let's go ahead and get started on chapter three."],[353.29,"And I, brethren, could not speak to you as to spiritual people. but as to carnal, as to babes in Christ"],[362.03,"So now we're getting some more tough love."],[364.61,"He's saying, I couldn't come to you."],[366.53,"You know, he's talking about the spiritual man and the person who has the spirit."],[370.13,"He's already said the mature."],[372.15,"There is wisdom for the mature here."],[374.93,"He says, now you may be saying to yourself, Well, I didn't think St."],[377.97,"Paul taught me any great stuff."],[380.7,"He said, That's because I couldn't."],[383.16,"Because you're not that mature person."],[387.08,"In Christ. You're a new creation in Christ, regeneration."],[391.16,"You've been born again, and you're still infants."],[394.26,"You're still in your infancy."],[395.7,"So I couldn't teach you any of this stuff yet."],[398.18,"And I still do"],[399.82,"I had to speak to you where you're at."],[404.27,"Right. Until you come to maturity."],[407.71,"I can understand these things."],[409.79,"I fed you with milk and not with solid food."],[412.67,"For until now you are not able to receive it."],[415.15,"And even now you are still not able."],[418.99,"So he says, you know, it's like a baby."],[422.11,"You can't just shove a carrot in his mouth."],[424.45,"He's not going to be able to eat it."],[426.43,"I had to couldn't give you meat."],[428.91,"I was just giving you the milk."],[430.61,"To nourish you, keep you alive, help you come to maturity when you can handle the other."],[436.45,"You're still not there."],[437.65,"But now notice why they're not there."],[439.57,"For you are still carnal, carnal meaning you're still fleshly."],[441.89,"Your body is your physicality"],[443.27,"Remember how St."],[443.99,"Paul uses flesh."],[445.03,"Flesh and body are two different things."],[449.03,"Your flesh is sort of all the corrupt sinfulness that's in you."],[454.03,"So when you when you die in this world for St."],[458.51,"Paul, the flesh dies."],[461.6,"And it's your body, your physical body that's raised in the resurrection."],[466.48,"We'll get into that more in in chapter 15."],[472.4,"But what does he mean that they're fleshly?"],[474.48,"For where there are where there are is added."],[479.04,"For where envy, strife, and divisions are among you, are you not carnal, fleshly, and behaving like men?"],[488.38,"Now, the word men there is talking about humans."],[491.66,"Because remember what he's just said."],[493.58,"Remember what he said back at the beginning."],[495.34,"They were fighting."],[496.46,"And that they were saints."],[498.22,"They're called to be holy ones, like the angels."],[501.6,"He says, You ain't behaving like angels."],[504.96,"You're behaving very much like men, like people of this world in this age."],[509.12,"That's how you're behaving."],[511.04,"And so their immaturity is expressed in envy, strife, divisions."],[515.62,"So this is when St."],[516.82,"Paul's talking about maturity, this is living by the Spirit."],[520.27,"This is living your life in a certain way."],[522.27,"That's the evidence of having come to maturity."],[525.69,"As long as there's all this nonsense going on."],[527.77,"Now we have to remember they didn't have the same view of children in the ancient world that we do"],[533.87,"We tend to look at small children as just sort of angelic and cute and wonderful."],[540.01,"They looked at them not the way that we look at our kids."],[542.65,"They looked at them at the way we look at other people's kids."],[548.01,"You know, and and the reality is that small children are unbelievably selfish, self-centered, brutish, easily angered, throw tantrums."],[558.97,"Yes. Like Hobbes' life, yeah."],[564.73,"You know, they they were right right?"],[567.33,"And that's what when when uh St."],[570.41,"Paul's calling them infants, that's what he's talking about."],[571.77,"He's not saying you're cherubic and innocent"],[574.53,"He's saying envy, stri't, you're completely, you know, immature in that sense."],[580.69,"Immature behavior in that sense."],[582.53,"One of my favorite quotes from St."],[583.89,"Augustine is he talks about how when he was an infant, the only thing that stopped him from sinning was the weakness of his limbs."],[592.93,"I had trouble getting around, so I couldn't sin as much as I wanted to."],[598.21,"But so that's that's the idea here."],[600.13,"He says, you know, where that's going on, there's no maturity."],[603.49,"There's no maturity."],[604.77,"Well, one says, I am of Paul, and another, I am of Apollos, are you not fleshly?"],[609.59,"Going back to where he started this."],[611.27,"If if you are so ignorant as to think that way, how can I go deeper with you?"],[617.8,"If you haven't even got this very basic stuff, of what I preached."],[623.82,"And so he then continues, Who then is Paul and who is Apollos, but ministers through whom you believed, as the Lord gave to each one."],[632.54,"I planted, Apollos watered, but God gave the increase."],[636.94,"So then neither he who plants is anything, nor he who waters, but God who gives the increase."],[642.54,"Now he him who plants and he who waters are one, and each one will receive his own reward according to his own labor."],[649.74,"Okay, so he says, going back to this again."],[652.86,"You say, Well, I'm of Paul and I'm of Apollos."],[654.62,"He says, Look, I came there and I planted."],[656.32,"He planted the church."],[657.28,"This is part of where we get the language of church planting."],[660.12,"It was like I was planting seeds"],[660.42,"St. Paul says, I came, I still I helped get the community together and help get the community started."],[667.06,"And then Apollos came through, he watered."],[670.76,"He watered what I had planted to help cultivate it."],[673.97,"But as anyone who's a farmer knows, and most of these people are engaged at some level with farming."],[679.95,"So any farmer knows you can plant all the seeds you want, you can water and irrigate and stuff as much as you want, but it's not up to you what grows."],[692.35,"You can't force the crops to grow."],[695.55,"There's another level to this in terms of what we were just saying."],[699.39,"Does anybody remember what who Demeter was?"],[702.43,"Demoner is the goddess of the harvest."],[703.71,"Of the harvest"],[707.35,"So the mysteries and all of that surrounds the idea of securing a bountiful harvest through rituals and through the worship of these spiritual powers."],[719.83,"Paul's even poking that a little bit here."],[722.55,"But it's not her, it's God who brings the increase."],[727.51,"So even his analogy, he's sort of poking at that a little bit."],[731.67,"So who do you give thanks to for the increase?"],[735.59,"Not Paul, not Apollos, not the farmer."],[738.73,"Not the guy who planted the seeds, not the guy who dug the irrigation ditch."],[742.17,"Or Demeter. Or Demeter."],[744.41,"You give the thanks to God."],[745.69,"He's the one who did it."],[746.83,"St. Paul's saying in the same situation. in your community"],[749.83,"And he says, you know, about himself and Apollos."],[753.77,"He's especially not trying to, I mean, he'll slam himself to a certain extent, but he's not slamming Saint Apollos."],[759.46,"He says, look, we're workers."],[761.06,"He says, the workers, they get their reward."],[763.3,"They get paid."],[764.5,"The guy who's out there doing that, they get paid when the harvest comes."],[768.12,"So St. Paul says, look, we're gonna get our reward from God."],[771.96,"St. Who brought the increase."],[773.88,"Meaning, I definitely don't need you to give me credit."],[777.72,"My reward's from God."],[779.4,"He's the one that paid me."],[780.44,"He's the one you should be thanking."],[781.8,"He's the one who who bro brougughtht the increase."],[785.64,"For we are God's fellow workers."],[787.96,"We meaning he and St."],[789.64,"Apollos. You are God's field."],[791.88,"According to the grace of God which was given to me"],[792.08,"You are God's building."],[796.32,"Now he's changing his metaphor."],[798.5,"He says, You're the field."],[800.26,"Now you're like a building."],[805.11,"According to the grace of God which was given to me, as a wise master builder, I have laid the foundation and another builds on it."],[811.99,"But let each one take heed how he builds on it."],[815.27,"So he says, Look, I showed up, switching our metaphors, you're like a building."],[819.43,"I showed I laid a foundation."],[822.15,"Say Apollos came and he built on it."],[824.63,"But you notice, even when he says that he came and laid a foundation, he says, according to the grace that God given me."],[829.93,"Remember, grace is God working in his creation."],[833.69,"So St. Paul is saying, I'm not taking you credit for laying the foundation."],[835.29,"God, I'm his fellow worker, his co-worker"],[841.81,"Literally synergy. That's the word he's using."],[846.3,"I was working, but he's the one who's laid the foundation."],[848.78,"He did it through me."],[850.04,"And then he built on it through Saint Apollos."],[854.06,"And now, in this switch metaphor, he's about to say, and now all of you in the community are building together."],[863.36,"There was the foundation, there was the beginnings of it, and now you're building, working toward bringing this to this work in Corinth to completion."],[872.56,"That's why he says, Let each one take heed how he builds on it."],[876.14,"He's saying, everything that you're doing now is building."],[878.14,"Building on that on that foundation"],[883.94,"For no other foundation can anyone lay than that which is laid, which is Jesus Christ."],[893.22,"So when he says he laid a foundation, that's what he means."],[895.86,"I preach the gospel to you."],[897.62,"I preach Christ to you."],[898.9,"You can't go and lay another foundation somewhere and try and build something else."],[903.06,"Whether that's your local Demoner temple, whether that's you know, with your stoic buddies down at the Agora."],[909.74,"You can't go and lay this other foundation."],[911.82,"You've got to build on this one."],[913.14,"You're building on this one that I laid, which is Christ."],[917.1,"Now, if anyone builds on this foundation with gold, silver, precious stones, wood, hay, straw. each one's work will become clear, for the day will declare it"],[926.66,"Because it will be revealed by fire, and the fire will test each one's work of what sort it is."],[932.58,"Okay. So he's including himself in this."],[936.24,"He says, I laid the foundation."],[937.92,"See, Apollos came and built on it."],[939.82,"He just used the metaphor of them receiving a reward for their work in the field."],[944.38,"This is the same kind of thing."],[945.58,"He says, I laid a foundation, we built, now you're building."],[949.26,"And what's going to happen is on the day, he's referring to the day of the Lord."],[952.86,"Capital D. Yeah, that's why they gave it a capital D."],[956.12,"It's not just daylight."],[957.98,"Or a day."],[959.5,"But this is referring to the day of the Lord."],[961.5,"Day of the Lord of the Old Testament is when God comes to visit his people."],[965.18,"And when God visits his people, it's not grandpa coming by for scones and tea."],[971.58,"It's more like wait till your father gets home."],[978.54,"Things are going to get resolved."],[979.82,"This is what we were talking about earlier."],[981.26,"He's going to be present in all his holiness, in all his glory."],[985.92,"He's going to become present."],[987.6,"And as St."],[988.4,"Paul says here, everything that we've built, including him, including Apollos, including the people in the community court, everything that we've built is going to be tried by fire."],[997.92,"We're going to put the fire to it."],[999.72,"And if you that sounds like one of the verses the Roman Catholics used to defend purgatory."],[1004.4,"Yeah, which, as we're going to see, doesn't really work."],[1006.8,"But Because, but anyway, so he says, look, some people are going to build with gold and jewels and precious gems and metals, those things, blast them with fire, you're all good."],[1019.57,"Some people are going to build with wood, hay, stubble, thatch."],[1023.89,"And then what's going to happen when those are subjected to fire?"],[1026.53,"They're gone. They're gone."],[1028.29,"They're gone. If anyone's work which is built on it endures, he will receive a reward."],[1033.41,"If anyone's work is burned, he will suffer loss."],[1036.21,"But he himself will be saved, yet so is through fire."],[1039.81,"Is he talking about who goes to heaven and who goes to hell?"],[1044.13,"No. No. In fact, St."],[1046.59,"Paul is never going to talk about who goes to heaven and who goes to hell, because that's not how he sees things."],[1050.99,"But he's going to talk about who's going to have life, be be. resurrected and live in the new heavens and the new earth of the presence of God, and then who's going to condemned at that same resurrection"],[1061.75,"That's how he's going to talk about it, not heaven and hell."],[1064.55,"But the point would be that's not that's not even what he's talking about here."],[1067.83,"Yeah, because he says the guys whose work gets burned will still be not destroyed."],[1074.56,"So he's talking about reward."],[1077.77,"He's talking about what we receive in that life to come."],[1083.55,"That's what we do in this life makes a difference."],[1086.59,"This is this is something we have uh tended as American Christians to get very much away from because we have this whole go to heaven, go to hell idea."],[1096.75,"And so it's like, I just have to hit this bar so I go to heaven."],[1097.63,"And then and then I'm all good"],[1103.25,"But that's not at all the way the kingdom is talked about by Christ in the gospels."],[1108.29,"I mean, how many times does he talk about your reward will be great in heaven?"],[1112.21,"God who rewards in secret will reward you openly."],[1114.77,"He who has been faithful with a little will be given much."],[1117.57,"Over and over and over."],[1121.14,"I mean, it's constant."],[1122.92,"It's constant. And he and on the flip side."],[1126.77,"The one who who does and teaches one of these to just disregard the least of these commandments will be least in the kingdom of heaven."],[1134.61,"He doesn't say we'll go to hell."],[1136.93,"He said, but we'll be least in the kingdom of heaven."],[1139.73,"And so this isn't material reward."],[1142.89,"We can take this too literally."],[1145.5,"We can take this the Muslim way and say, how many virgins do you get?"],[1148.62,"But that's not our concept of heaven, is this material place."],[1152.22,"It's not like, well, I'm going to have a bigger mansion in the new heavens and the new earth than you."],[1156.43,"Because that's no more true."],[1157.95,"That's no more true in the age to come than it is in this age."],[1161.39,"St. Paul's already pretty well refuted it for this age."],[1164.61,"That it's sort of these material things."],[1167.35,"This is this reward is our knowledge and closeness to God."],[1172.56,"Our place in Christ's kingdom."],[1174.82,"What he shares with us."],[1177.86,"And so this is this is why we have an understanding."],[1181.38,"Oh, I'll just go for it."],[1184.14,"In Western understandings of Christianity, both Roman Catholic and Protestant, there's this idea that there's a bar that you reach."],[1193.64,"And that gets you into heaven."],[1195.78,"You gotta hit the bar."],[1197.22,"They disagree about how you hit the bar."],[1200.76,"They generally agree, at least in theological systems, that you have to pile up a certain amount of merit with God, which works sort of like currency."],[1211.24,"And if you pile up enough of it, you're in."],[1214.2,"Okay In the Roman Catholic system, there's a whole bunch of different ways you can get it."],[1219.73,"The friends I was with last Sunday were actually talking about."],[1223.09,"Yeah. There's a whole bunch of different ways you can get it."],[1225.25,"They've got all kinds, I won't go. too far into there's conduct condyne merit and congruent merit, and there's all these different ways you can get it"],[1231.69,"But you could get it by doing particular things, by doing particular acts."],[1235.47,"Uh prayers, all different ways you can get it."],[1238.59,"You pile up enough, you're in."],[1240.35,"You can actually pile up extra, that's what the saints do in the Roman Catholic system."],[1244.27,"And so since they've got extra, they can pass that on to other people on earth to help them get up and hit the bar."],[1254.97,"And get in."],[1256.49,"The Protestant Reformation did not reject that idea of salvation by merit."],[1262.33,"What the Protestant Reformation said was Christ earns all the merit for you and gives it to you."],[1268.97,"That's what's called the active obedience of Christ in their system"],[1274.93,"Christ keeps the law perfectly, gives all that righteousness obedience to you, boom, one lump sum."],[1281.35,"Now you've got enough and you're in."],[1289.09,"And all his righteousness gets taken and put on."],[1290.77,"You just have to say the magic words."],[1292.37,"But both, they're about hitting this bar."],[1295.73,"In the Orthodox understanding of salvation, there is no bar."],[1300.29,"There is a continuum of the knowledge of God, the understanding of God, drawing closer to Christ and being conformed to his likeness."],[1309.57,"Christ is infinite"],[1310.33,"Because God is infinite."],[1316.41,"He is not finite."],[1317.53,"You're never going to get there."],[1321.29,"You're never going to be Christ."],[1324.01,"No matter how Christlike you become."],[1326.49,"You're never going to become what He is by nature."],[1329.13,"You're never going to be identical to God, no matter how."],[1332.9,"There's an infinite distance."],[1334.18,"And so there's an infinite continuum, and we make an infinite progress in the faith."],[1338.9,"There's not a point where we've arrived."],[1342.1,"And so, because of that, we not only have an understanding that in the kingdom, in the age to come, we're going to continue to grow in the knowledge of God."],[1351.46,"We're going to continue to grow closer."],[1352.98,"We're never going to exhaust the depths of of who who God is."],[1358.58,"But that makes sense of this reward language."],[1359.3,"That makes sense of this reward language"],[1364.44,"When the apostles asks Christ, you know, what about us who have given up our families and our jobs and our homes and everything to follow you, you know, ultimately their lives literally."],[1375.58,"When they're martyred, and he says, you'll be repaid."],[1378.54,"He's not saying, I'm going to give you ten families."],[1383.35,"He's saying that's the knowledge of God, the closest to Christ, all of those things which last forever."],[1390.33,"Are going to be deepened for you in proportion to how you have how you have done these things."],[1398.02,"How you've done these things."],[1399.78,"And for someone who actually loves Christ, that's the greatest reward you can have."],[1405.36,"Is to be closer to him, be more like him, know him more deeply."],[1411.54,"So that's the reward that's being talking talked about here."],[1414.34,"So St. Paul is saying to them, not just he's he's already done the negative side."],[1419.3,"You guys are a bunch of babies."],[1421.32,"You're a bunch of angry, tantrum throwing, jealous."],[1427.62,"Babies, babies. That's who you are."],[1430.83,"Now, this is the positive side."],[1433.33,"And with the field metaphor, he talked about, hey, this is my role."],[1435.81,"I'm just coming at planting."],[1437.25,"But we're gonna be rewarded for that."],[1439.01,"Now he's saying, you have that same opportunity."],[1442.13,"Here's another reason why you shouldn't be a Paul fan."],[1443.65,"Or an Apollos devotee"],[1449.83,"Is you have the same opportunity he does and that I do by walking by the Spirit, by following Christ, by drawing closer to him."],[1457.03,"You can build something in your life and in your community there in Corinth that will last for all of eternity in your lives and the lives of others."],[1465.27,"That's the opportunity you have."],[1467.19,"And instead you're piling up this garbage on the foundation I lay, which is gonna get wiped out, you know, when the time comes."],[1476.79,"When this age ends, which he's already been talking about."],[1480.01,"When this age ends, that all that garbage is gone."],[1483.45,"All this fleshly stuff you're doing, that's all gone."],[1486.97,"That's all dead."],[1487.77,"As opposed to what you could"],[1488.37,"It's all burned away."],[1490.13,"And you're gonna have nothing to show for it."],[1494.35,"And so St."],[1495.47,"Paul is not only inviting them to that, but he's giving sort of his motivation."],[1499.63,"Why does he do why is he doing what he does?"],[1502.91,"It must have seemed hard for St."],[1504.67,"Paul a lot of the time."],[1507.71,"Because, yeah, he planted a lot of churches, but as we can tell from his epistles, things didn't go well."],[1514.51,"Like, if if you were sent out, even I dare to say, by the missions department of one of the Orthodox uh uh archdioceses in this country, and you went out and planted a bunch of uh of churches like St."],[1529.95,"Paul did, and they had the kind of problems within the first few years that these churches had."],[1532.51,"You get fired"],[1537.99,"They'd say to you as a priest, they'd say, You're not cut out for church planting."],[1543.44,"It's you know, maybe it's a we need to put you in some other kind of ministry."],[1548.1,"We need to put you in some other kind of because clearly the gift is over."],[1552.95,"Okay, there are lots of problems, you know."],[1555.27,"But Saint Paul, why does he keep going?"],[1557.91,"Why does he even write these letters?"],[1561.03,"Why doesn't he just say, Shut it down, I'll try somewhere else."],[1565.12,"You know, why doesn't he do that?"],[1569.22,"Because this is why he's doing it."],[1571.7,"He's not working for them, he's not trying to make them happy."],[1574.42,"y. His pay at the end of the da is going to come from God"],[1574.94,"He's serving God."],[1575.98,"He's working for God."],[1581.58,"And so he's going to keep doing the work, even if it's not quote unquote successful, according to the wisdom of this world."],[1590.54,"I want to ask a question."],[1593.82,"If anyone's work is burned, he will suffer loss, but he himself will be saved yet so as through fire."],[1600.67,"Can you expound on that a bit?"],[1603.39,"That's that's referring to that concept that we were talking about earlier about God's holiness and his glory burning away the fleshly part, the carnal part, the fleshly part, the sinful part."],[1616.11,"He himself would be saved to me like he gets into heaven."],[1618.43,"And I know that's not that's not"],[1623.99,"You just told me that's not what it means."],[1626.39,"He himself is preserved."],[1627.75,"Uh-huh. He isn't burned up."],[1629.91,"He's not saying you're gonna get consumed."],[1632.79,"Uh-huh. You're gonna be burned up."],[1634.45,"You don't cease to exist."],[1635.97,"You're gonna survive, but you're gonna go through a fire."],[1638.61,"Uh-huh. But through a fire, that implies that you're it's not pleasant."],[1643.47,"Yeah, but you're gonna come out."],[1644.67,"You're gonna come out."],[1645.47,"Yes, you're not gonna die in the fire."],[1647.07,"Uh huh. You're not gonna be burned up with your sins."],[1649.65,"Uh huh. That's the language that's used in those the day of the Lord is when all things will be tried by fire."],[1656.29,"Those passages in the prophets in the Old Testament."],[1658.53,"They talk about people being consumed with their sins."],[1662.13,"You say that that's I'm he's not threatening them with."],[1662.69,"'s. He not threatening them with that"],[1668.41,"But he's he's telling them you have this opportunity."],[1671.45,"So these people to do so much more."],[1675.77,"Why isn't this purgatory then?"],[1678.01,"These people get because he's not talking about going, he's not talking about going to a place for a period of time to suffer to make up for the sins they committed that they haven't repented of properly."],[1688.91,"Which is what purgatory is."],[1694.99,"On the day when Christ judges the living and the dead."],[1698.19,"Uh-huh This happens."],[1700.11,"Everything is tried by fire."],[1701.71,"Uh huh. And all this garbage, all this fleshly garbage, assuming you're you've received the the Holy Spirit, and you're following Christ, all garbage in your life is gonna get burned away."],[1714.06,"All the sin, all the contamination, all the uncleanness, all that's gonna get burned away."],[1719.5,"For everybody. Uh-huh."],[1720.86,"For everybody. He's saying the way you guys are going right now, you're not gonna have much left."],[1727.18,"Uh-huh. When all that's burned away."],[1729.24,"But you have the opportunity to build things now, to do things now, to create things now that will last through that fire into the age to come."],[1739.88,"Your goal shouldn't be to sort of stumble naked into the kingdom of heaven."],[1748.52,"So that's that's what he's talking about."],[1749.48,"'s what he's talking about. That"],[1752.24,"For all of us, that's gonna be, but wouldn't it be better to not waste your life on all this garbage that's just gonna disappear and come to nothing when you could be investing it."],[1763.78,"When you could be doing things now that make a difference in eternity."],[1768.92,"Does it make a lot of sense to waste it?"],[1773.08,"Which is what they're doing with all their silly arguments about who's better, Paul or Apollos."],[1779.82,"Although I will spend hours debating the fact, and I say fact, that Captain Kirk is better than Captain Picard."],[1789.9,"Just to clarify."],[1791.66,"That is not a vain dispute."],[1793.34,"That is the truth that everyone needs to hear"],[1801.14,"He says, Do you not know that you are the temple of God?"],[1804.66,"And that the Spirit of God dwells in you."],[1807.54,"If anyone defiles the temple of God, God will destroy him."],[1811.54,"For the temple of God is holy, which temple you are."],[1816.66,"This is actually, I know the Orthodox Study Bible has grouped this in as the last part of the last section."],[1821.86,"It's actually the lead into the next section."],[1823.94,"Uh-huh. Uh where now he's going to chide them a little more."],[1831.46,"So he's already said you've received the Holy Spirit."],[1835.22,"You've received the Holy Spirit, so you have access to all these things."],[1838.5,"And he's just said, you'll be saved as though by fire."],[1841.6,"Uh-huh. So he wants to make clear, I'm not saying, okay, now you've got the Holy Spirit, so you're good."],[1848.86,"That's not what I'm saying."],[1850.14,"Because the fact that you have the Holy Spirit dwelling with you, the Holy Spirit is the same presence of God that dwelt in the temple."],[1857.58,"Solomon's temple, at least."],[1859.9,"That got destroyed."],[1861.18,"But but it's always if that makes you that makes you the temple of God, your flesh."],[1867.26,"Or not your flesh, your body."],[1869.16,"Your body. Because he dwells in you."],[1871.8,"So he says, Look, what happens to someone who goes and defiles the temple of God?"],[1878.76,"Oh they,'re less"],[1882.28,"This is very bad."],[1882.92,"And this is something, this is something, again, that the pagans would have understood"],[1888.77,"One of the worst things you could be in the Roman world was a defiler of temples."],[1893.81,"When you see lists of just horrible people."],[1896.71,"Like their version of just the we would say, like, what, serial killers, Nazis."],[1901.29,"Those would be our like Rome's most horrible."],[1904.23,"That's that's who we'd compare somebody to."],[1906.15,"We'd say somebody's like the Nazis, or we'd say somebody's like a serial killer or a child molester or something."],[1911.37,"That for us would be."],[1912.81,"You look at their their lists in the Greco Roman world, and very high on the list."],[1919.13,"Like Aristotle's list was people who kill pregnant women and their unborn children, and people who defile temples."],[1930.37,"Yes. That gives you an idea."],[1934.53,"Says that in the Nicobachean ethics, you can look it up if you really want to."],[1937.89,"These are the people who you just can't morally educate for him."],[1940.37,"They have to be killed or enslaved."],[1942.93,"But people who defile temples are at the very bottom."],[1947.73,"You read the Iliad, anybody remember why Achilles dies in the Iliad?"],[1952.61,"Because he defiled a temple."],[1955.09,"This is like the worst thing you can do from a pagan perspective."],[1960.21,"And then along comes some Christian martyrs and do defile the temples and get martyred."],[1965.49,"Yeah. You defile the temple."],[1967.1,"Then on the flip side, because he does have some Jewish audience there."],[1972.5,"So when they hear about defiling the temple of God, who are they thinking of?"],[1975.78,"They're thinking of the Romans."],[1976.98,"Antiochus Epiphanes. Who defiled the temple and they couldn't use it."],[1983.19,"The Maccabean Revolt happened."],[1985.43,"So they also."],[1988.55,"Yeah, this is about the most horrible thing you could do."],[1990.95,"And death and destruction comes out of that."],[1993.51,"You're right around this time."],[1994.87,"This is where the Romans would pray to your dude."],[1999.59,"Do we go to a country they were about to invade and pray to that country's God?"],[2003.35,"And give offerings to that country's God."],[2007.99,"So to just this is this is really like don't go and defile a temple."],[2013.67,"This is the ultimate. insult to the entire and so and so St"],[2019.63,"Paul is saying, yes, Holy Spirit, good side."],[2024.97,"Good side. You have the Spirit of God dwelling with you."],[2027.29,"You have access to all the riches of the knowledge of God."],[2029.93,"All of these good things."],[2031.69,"But that also means you're the temple of the Holy Spirit."],[2034.73,"What you do now in and to and through your body can defile that temple."],[2041.29,"Implied, and we all know what happens when you defile a temple."],[2046.73,"We all know what happens."],[2050.73,"For the temple of God is holy, which temple you are."],[2054.89,"He's already called them holy, remember at the beginning"],[2057.69,"This is what you're called to be."],[2058.49,"to be He's saying this is why you need."],[2058.73,"And he's going to build off this now"],[2066.37,"In his discussion of uh he's talked about the factions."],[2069.89,"He's going to start getting into uh he's going to start getting into some of the uh gross sins that are going on uh in Corinth at this time."],[2080.77,"Uh so that's a good teacher."],[2082.85,"Yeah, I think this is a good place to uh end for tonight."],[2085.57,"So thank you, everybody."],[2086.93,"Thank you. Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2096.77,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancient faith.com."],[2102.13,"That's whole counsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":20.96,"lv":2,"h":"2:13-16 - Spiritual vs. natural; the mind of Christ","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>2:13</b>: not in words <b>man's wisdom</b> teaches, but the <b>Holy Spirit</b> teaches; <b>2:14-16</b>: natural man doesn't receive the things of the Spirit - <b>foolishness</b>, <b>spiritually discerned</b>; spiritual man judges all, judged by none; \"who has known the <b>mind of the Lord</b>?\" - we have the <b>mind of Christ</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Wisdom man's word teaches\" = <b>philosophy</b></li><li class=\"d1\">philosophers might cheer his critique of paganism - \"all nonsense, we're more enlightened\" - <b>they don't have it either</b>; they can't perceive it</li><li class=\"d0\">English <b>rarely capitalizes</b> spiritual</li><li class=\"d1\">we hear <b>Marianne Williamson</b>, crystal power, \"watered down Gnostic nonsense\", New Age</li><li class=\"d1\">Bible: spiritual = of the <b>Spirit</b>, capital S, the <b>Holy Spirit</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Philosophers can tell you about the <b>natural man</b> and natural world</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Aristotle's Parts of Animals</b> - closest to science in 4th c. BC Greece</li><li class=\"d1\">can't tell the things of the Spirit: truths from the <b>age to come</b>, no access</li><li class=\"d0\">Seem <b>foolishness</b> - they laugh at you, but <b>can't judge</b> you: who are they to judge the <b>mind of God</b>?</li><li class=\"d1\">any philosopher: can a <b>human brain</b> judge God's mind? - logically <b>no</b></li></ul>"},{"t":198.2,"lv":3,"h":"The mind of Christ; seeking in the wrong place","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Mind\" is not your <b>brain</b> - it's the <b>mind of Christ</b>, because the Holy Spirit dwells in you</li><li class=\"d1\">Spirit of God = Spirit of Christ → knows mind of Christ and of God → <b>you have access</b></li><li class=\"d0\">A philosopher without the Spirit can't judge - like an <b>eight-year-old judging your calculus</b></li><li class=\"d0\">They've been <b>digging in the wrong place</b> - wisdom isn't there</li><li class=\"d1\">it's in the <b>Holy Spirit in you</b>, <b>freely given</b></li><li class=\"d1\">mystery initiations: <b>large sums of money</b>; Paul didn't <b>charge to baptize</b> or preach</li><li class=\"d0\">Nothing about Paul to recommend him - not a <b>hugely successful life</b></li><li class=\"d1\">infomercial guys with money-making secrets: \"on a boat with a couple of models\"</li><li class=\"d1\">his lifestyle was <b>pretty lousy</b>, and he was open about it</li><li class=\"d0\">What he gave is <b>ultimate value</b>; where they look in Corinth: nothing but <b>destruction</b></li></ul>"},{"t":346.89,"lv":2,"h":"3:1-4 - Babes in Christ","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Little time left → start <b>chapter 3</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:1-2</b>: could not speak to you as <b>spiritual</b> but as <b>carnal</b>, <b>babes in Christ</b>; fed <b>milk, not solid food</b> - not able, and <b>still not</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Tough love</b>: \"I didn't think Paul taught me any great stuff\" - because <b>you're not mature</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>new creation</b>, regeneration, born again - <b>still infants</b></li><li class=\"d1\">baby: can't shove a <b>carrot</b> in his mouth; milk keeps you alive until maturity</li><li class=\"d0\">Why: still <b>carnal</b> = <b>fleshly</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul's <b>flesh vs. body</b> - different things</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>flesh</b> = corrupt sinfulness; at death the flesh dies; the <b>body</b> is raised (ch. 15)</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:3</b>: where <b>envy, strife, divisions</b>, you're fleshly and behaving <b>like men</b> (= humans)</li><li class=\"d1\">called to be <b>holy ones, like the angels</b> - behaving like people of this age</li><li class=\"d1\">immaturity shown in <b>envy, strife, divisions</b>; maturity = <b>living by the Spirit</b></li></ul>"},{"t":527.77,"lv":3,"h":"Infants in the ancient world","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Ancients didn't see children as we do - \"the way we look at <b>other people's kids</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">small children: <b>selfish, self-centered, brutish</b>, easily angered, tantrums - Hobbes</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul's \"infants\" doesn't mean <b>cherubic and innocent</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Augustine</b>: as an infant, only thing stopping him from sinning was <b>weakness of his limbs</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:4</b>: \"I am of Paul\" / \"I am of Apollos\" - <b>fleshly</b></li><li class=\"d1\">if so ignorant, <b>how can I go deeper</b>? Haven't got the <b>basics</b> of what I preached</li></ul>"},{"t":623.82,"lv":2,"h":"3:5-9a - Planting and watering","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:5-8</b>: Paul and Apollos <b>ministers through whom you believed</b>; <b>I planted, Apollos watered, God gave the increase</b>; each <b>rewarded for own labor</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Paul <b>planted</b> the church - origin of \"<b>church planting</b>\"; Apollos <b>watered</b> and cultivated</li><li class=\"d1\">farmers know: <b>can't force the crops to grow</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Another level: <b>Demeter</b> = goddess of the <b>harvest</b></li><li class=\"d1\">mysteries aim at securing <b>bountiful harvest</b> through ritual</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul pokes at that: <b>God</b> brings the increase</li><li class=\"d0\">Who to thank? Not Paul, Apollos, the farmer, ditch-digger, or <b>Demeter</b> - <b>God</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not slamming <b>Apollos</b>: \"we're workers\"</li><li class=\"d1\">workers <b>get paid at harvest</b> - reward <b>from God</b>, so \"I don't need you to give me credit\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:9</b>: <b>God's fellow workers</b> - field, then <b>building</b></li></ul>"},{"t":791.88,"lv":2,"h":"3:9b-11 - Foundation and building","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:9-10</b>: \"<b>God's building</b>\" - metaphor switch; <b>wise master builder</b>, laid the <b>foundation</b>, another builds on it; <b>take heed how</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Even \"grace given to me\": <b>grace = God working in his creation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not taking credit - \"<b>co-worker</b>\" = literally <b>synergy</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God laid the foundation through Paul, built on it through <b>Apollos</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Now <b>all of you</b> are building together toward completing the work in Corinth</li><li class=\"d1\">\"everything you're doing now is <b>building</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:11</b>: no other foundation than <b>Jesus Christ</b></li><li class=\"d1\">= he preached the gospel, preached <b>Christ</b></li><li class=\"d1\">can't lay another foundation: <b>local Demeter temple</b>, <b>Stoic buddies</b> at the Agora</li></ul>"},{"t":917.1,"lv":2,"h":"3:12-15 - Tried by fire","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:12-15</b>: gold, silver, precious stones, <b>wood, hay, straw</b>; work revealed by <b>fire</b>; if endures → <b>reward</b>; burned → <b>loss</b>, yet <b>saved as through fire</b></li><li class=\"d0\">He includes <b>himself</b>: laid foundation, Apollos built, now you build</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>The Day</b> = <b>Day of the Lord</b> (capital D)</li><li class=\"d1\">God visits his people: \"not grandpa coming by for <b>scones and tea</b>\" - \"<b>wait till your father gets home</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">present in <b>holiness and glory</b>; everything built, including Paul and Apollos, <b>tried by fire</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Sounds like a <b>purgatory</b> proof text - \"as we'll see, doesn't really work\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Gold and jewels: blasted with fire, <b>all good</b>; wood, hay, stubble, thatch: <b>gone</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Q: heaven or hell? - <b>No</b>; Paul <b>never</b> talks that way</li><li class=\"d1\">he talks about who is <b>resurrected</b> to live in the <b>new heavens and new earth</b> vs. <b>condemned</b> at that same resurrection</li><li class=\"d1\">here: those whose work burns <b>aren't destroyed</b> → about <b>reward</b>, what we receive in the life to come</li></ul>"},{"t":1083.55,"lv":3,"h":"Reward language vs. the American \"go to heaven\" bar","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>What we do in this life makes a difference</b></li><li class=\"d0\">American Christians: \"hit this bar so I <b>go to heaven</b>, then I'm all good\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Not how Christ talks: <b>reward great in heaven</b>; God who rewards in secret; faithful with little given much</li><li class=\"d1\">flip side: whoever relaxes <b>least commandments</b> will be <b>least in the kingdom</b> - doesn't say hell</li><li class=\"d0\">Not <b>material</b> reward: not \"how many virgins\" (Muslim way), not a <b>bigger mansion</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not true in this age (Paul refuted it); not in the age to come</li><li class=\"d0\">Reward = <b>knowledge of and closeness to God</b>, our place in Christ's kingdom, <b>what he shares with us</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1177.86,"lv":3,"h":"Western merit vs. Orthodox continuum","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Roman Catholic and Protestant</b>: a <b>bar</b> you reach to get into heaven; disagree how</li><li class=\"d1\">both: pile up <b>merit</b> with God, like <b>currency</b></li><li class=\"d1\">RC: many ways - <b>condign and congruent merit</b>, acts, prayers; saints pile up <b>extra</b> to pass on to others</li><li class=\"d1\">Protestant Reformation didn't reject <b>salvation by merit</b>: <b>Christ earns it and gives it to you</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>active obedience of Christ</b>: keeps the law perfectly, righteousness transferred in <b>one lump sum</b> - \"say the magic words\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Orthodox</b>: <b>no bar</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>continuum</b> of knowledge of God, drawing closer, <b>conformed to his likeness</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God is <b>infinite</b> - never become Christ; <b>infinite distance</b>, infinite progress</li><li class=\"d1\">in the age to come we <b>keep growing</b>, never exhaust God</li><li class=\"d0\">Makes sense of <b>reward language</b>: apostles gave up families, jobs, lives - \"you'll be <b>repaid</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not <b>ten families</b>: knowledge of God, closeness to Christ <b>deepened in proportion</b></li><li class=\"d1\">for one who loves Christ, <b>greatest reward</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1411.54,"lv":2,"h":"Paul's motivation; what could last","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Negative side done: \"a bunch of <b>babies</b>\" - <b>angry, tantrum-throwing, jealous</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Positive side: <b>same opportunity</b> as Paul and Apollos by <b>walking by the Spirit</b></li><li class=\"d1\">build something in Corinth that <b>lasts for all eternity</b></li><li class=\"d1\">instead piling up <b>garbage</b> on the foundation - all the <b>fleshly stuff</b> burned away when this age ends; \"nothing to show\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Why does Paul keep going? Planted many churches, <b>problems</b> within years</li><li class=\"d1\">modern Orthodox <b>missions department</b> would say \"<b>you're not cut out for church planting</b>\" - fired</li><li class=\"d1\">why not <b>shut it down</b>, try elsewhere?</li><li class=\"d1\">he's <b>not working for them</b>, not trying to make them happy - <b>serving God</b>; pay comes <b>from God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">keeps working even if not \"successful\" by <b>wisdom of this world</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1590.54,"lv":2,"h":"Q&amp;A: \"saved as through fire\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: expound on <b>3:15</b> - \"he himself saved, yet so as through fire\"?</li><li class=\"d1\">God's <b>holiness and glory</b> burning away the <b>carnal, sinful</b> part</li><li class=\"d1\">Q: \"he gets into heaven\" - <b>he himself is preserved</b>, not burned up, <b>doesn't cease to exist</b></li><li class=\"d1\">through fire = <b>not pleasant</b>, but you <b>come out</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Day of the Lord</b> language of the prophets: <b>consumed with their sins</b> - Paul isn't threatening that</li><li class=\"d1\">Q: why not <b>purgatory</b>? - not a <b>place for a period</b> to suffer to make up for <b>sins not repented of properly</b></li><li class=\"d1\">on the day Christ judges, <b>everything tried by fire</b>; all fleshly garbage burned away <b>for everybody</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Corinth's way: <b>not much left</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Opportunity: build now what <b>lasts through the fire</b> into the age to come</li><li class=\"d1\">\"shouldn't <b>stumble naked</b> into the kingdom of heaven\"</li><li class=\"d1\">why <b>waste life</b> on silly arguments, Paul vs. Apollos - \"<b>Captain Kirk vs. Captain Picard</b>\" is not a vain dispute</li></ul>"},{"t":1801.14,"lv":2,"h":"3:16-17 - You are the temple of God","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>3:16-17</b>: you are the <b>temple of God</b>, Spirit dwells in you; <b>defile it, God will destroy him</b>; temple is <b>holy</b>, which you are</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Orthodox Study Bible</b> groups this with the last section - actually the <b>lead into the next section</b>: more chiding</li><li class=\"d0\">Not \"you've got the Spirit, so you're good\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Spirit = same <b>presence of God</b> that dwelt in <b>Solomon's temple</b> (destroyed)</li><li class=\"d1\">makes <b>your body</b> the temple (not flesh)</li><li class=\"d0\">What happens to one who <b>defiles the temple</b>?</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Pagans</b> understood: <b>temple-defiler</b> among worst in the Roman world</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Aristotle</b> (Nicomachean Ethics): killers of <b>pregnant women</b> and temple-defilers - can't be morally educated; <b>killed or enslaved</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Iliad</b>: <b>Achilles</b> dies for defiling a temple</li><li class=\"d1\">Romans prayed to the <b>god of a country</b> about to be invaded, gave offerings</li><li class=\"d1\">ironic: Christian <b>martyrs</b> defile temples and get martyred</li></ul>"},{"t":1965.49,"lv":3,"h":"Jewish hearers and holiness","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Jewish audience: defiling the temple = <b>Antiochus Epiphanes</b> → <b>Maccabean Revolt</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"most horrible thing you could do\" - <b>death and destruction</b> follow</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul: Holy Spirit = <b>good side</b> - access to <b>all riches of the knowledge of God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">also means <b>temple of the Holy Spirit</b>: what you do <b>in and through your body</b> can defile it</li><li class=\"d1\">\"we all know what happens\" when you defile a temple</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Temple of God is holy, which you are</b> - already called <b>holy</b> at the beginning</li><li class=\"d1\">\"this is <b>what you're called to be</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Next: <b>gross sins</b> going on in Corinth after the factions</li></ul>"}],"next":"Next: done with factions - starts on the <b>gross sins</b> going on in Corinth"});
